# Catalog hubs — host is generic

**Full model:** [forja-external-plugins-host.mdc](./forja-external-plugins-host.mdc) · **Playback:** [forja-playback-host-generic.mdc](./forja-playback-host-generic.mdc)

Hub packs (`plugins/hubs/**`) are **external plugins**. The Flutter host
(`apps/forja/lib/shared/catalog/**`, CatalogShell, `catalog_open`) must stay
**pack-agnostic**.

A hub pack may use **any** upstream catalog system (TMDB today, something else
tomorrow). The host must not assume which one.

## Forbidden in host catalog code

Hardcoding or branching on:

- Pack / plugin ids: `anilist`, `kisskh`, `kisskh-hub`, `arabic-hub`, `tmdb` (as plugin id), …
- Scraper / source names: `larozaa`, `dimatoon`, `brstej`, …
- Pack-specific `ids.*` keys to decide behavior (`numericId('anilist')`, `ids['larozaa']`, …)
- **Upstream API clients in the host** — no `TmdbApi`, no `getTvSeasonDetails`, no title
  search/match, no enrich logic keyed off `ids.tmdb` inside `shared/catalog/**`

**Wrong:** `switch (type) { case 'arabic': parse ids.larozaa / dimatoon / brstej }`  
**Wrong:** `openAnimeDetails` only if `numericId('anilist')`  
**Wrong:** `HubDetailsScreen` calling `TmdbApi().getRichDetails` / season stills / backdrop fetch  
**Wrong:** host `loadTmdbSeasonExtras` to patch `meta.videos` after details  
**Wrong:** seeding Feature docs / shell with scraper hostnames as Dart constants for open

### Allowed in host (render-only)

- Read **opaque fields** plugins already put on meta (`poster`, `background`, `videos`,
  `tmdbMediaType`, `ids` map) — do not interpret them to call upstream APIs
- `resolveHubCoverUrl` / `hubImageUrl` — turn plugin-supplied absolute URLs (or legacy
  relative paths) into loadable image URLs; no match/search/enrich
- `CatalogRuntime` **pipe enrich** — run companion plugin declared on source (`enrich` field);
  host merges returned `meta` / `items`; host does not implement enrich itself

## Enrich companions (plugin-owned)

Source plugins declare a companion, e.g. `"enrich": "anime-enrich-tmdb"`.

| Concern | Owner |
|--------|--------|
| Match upstream title → external id | `plugins/hubs/**/enrich_*.js` + `_kit.js` |
| Poster / backdrop / logo / synopsis | enrich plugin mutates `meta` |
| Episode `videos[].thumbnail` / title / overview | enrich plugin mutates `meta.videos` on `details` |
| Cast / trailers / recommendations rows | enrich plugin adds `details.rails` or meta fields — **not** host `TmdbApi` |
| Which upstream API (TMDB vs other) | **Only** the enrich plugin pack |

Host after `CatalogRuntime.run(action: details)`:

1. Use `envelope.meta` as returned (already piped through enrich).
2. Render `meta.videos` in episode picker — **no second upstream fetch**.

If enrich is disabled or pack uses another system, host still works with pack-only meta.

## Required contract

Plugins put a host **surface** on every openable meta:

```json
"open": {
  "surface": "anime" | "drama" | "tmdb" | "arabic",
  "id": "<opaque for that surface>",
  "...": "surface extras (arabic: source, url, movie; tmdb: mediaType)"
}
```

Host `openCatalogMetaItem` / list-pin helpers **only** switch on `open.surface`
(host feature routes). Opaque `open.id` + extras are passed through.

Allowed host id scheme (not a pack): **`tmdb`** for movie/tv when `open` is
absent and `type` is `movie`/`tv` (Home TMDB rows — not hub enrich).

## Where pack knowledge lives

| Layer | May know scrapers / pack ids / upstream APIs |
|-------|---------------------------------------------|
| `plugins/hubs/**` JS | Yes — emit `open`, layout, enrich |
| Host feature screens (`features/anime`, `asian_drama`, `arabic`, …) | Legacy only — **new hub work uses `shared/catalog` kit** |
| `shared/catalog/**`, CatalogShell open path | **No** |

## Seed / nav

`PluginNavRegistry` may cache last pack `nav` for flash-free boot.
Optional packs (Arabic) must not be special-cased
in open/list logic. Builders/destinations still come from pack `nav` on refresh.
Do **not** hardcode hub tab ids (`anime`, `asian_drama`, …) into
`PlatformDefaults` or empty `seedBuiltIns` — see [RFC-081](../../docs/rfc/fixed/081-[fixed]-host-only-platform-nav-defaults.md).

## When adding a hub

1. Emit `open` from the pack meta builder.
2. Put all upstream enrich (images, episode stills, extra rows) in the pack or its
   **enrich companion** — not in Dart host.
3. If a new **host surface** is needed, add one route handler — not scraper names.
4. Do **not** teach `catalog_open.dart` about the pack’s upstream sites.

## Legacy debt (do not extend)

`hub_details_sections.dart` still has `hubLoadTmdbRich` / `hubTmdbHeroBackdropUrls`
(host `TmdbApi`). **Do not add more.** New enrich belongs in plugins; migrate these
to pack-returned `rails` / meta when touched.
